Serif figure fonts: DejaVu Sans -> STIXGeneral (Times-metric), embedding kept.

PREPARED, NOT APPLIED. Settled by probe_figure_font.py (see its docstring).
Rationale in one line: the figures sit inline with a Times body and are set in
DejaVu Sans; STIXGeneral is Times-metric, ships with matplotlib, and stays an
EMBEDDED TrueType font, which template/neurips_2026.tex line 416 permits.

The mathtext.fontset line is REQUIRED, not decorative: fig2 and fig3 use
"$\Delta$", and without it matplotlib re-embeds DejaVuSans to draw that one
glyph, so the sans font never actually leaves the PDF (probe Part C). It is
added to fig1 too, which has no mathtext today, so a later "$...$" cannot
silently reintroduce it.

DO NOT APPLY YET. Changing the family changes text metrics, and each script's
_assert_no_text_overlaps (fig1:472, fig2:484, fig3:369) must still print
"TEXT OVERLAP CHECK: 0". Those scripts import _data.py, which correctly refuses
a partial cell while the irrigation ministral3:8b seed-44 no-validator run is
being written. Apply only after that run lands, then rebuild all three figures
and require 0 from each, then rerun submission_gate.py.

Apply with:  git apply SUBMISSION_2026/TAE/evidence/probe_figure_font.patch
Verify first: git apply --check SUBMISSION_2026/TAE/evidence/probe_figure_font.patch

